+# Bug Addendum v001: BlobWriteStream UTF-8 serialization
+
+## Metadata
+
+- Bug: `BUG-20260817-H7NP`
+- Verdict: `spec-gap`
+- Addendum version: `v001`
+- Effective date: `2026-08-27`
+- Status: approved
+- Human decision: automatic remediation authorization approved the evidence-based default verdict.
+
+## Target
+
+This addendum extends the Git Objects and Object Database blob/stream requirements. The original specifications remain unchanged.
+
+## Delta
+
+The existing requirements preserve blob content and streaming writes but do not define the byte encoding used by `BlobWriteStream.writeString`.
+
+## Normative Addition
+
+1. `BlobWriteStream.writeString` must encode its Dart `String` input as UTF-8 before sending bytes to the native write stream.
+2. The result of committing such a stream must preserve the UTF-8 byte sequence exactly.
+3. `BlobWriteStream.write` remains the raw-byte API and must not decode, transcode, or otherwise alter supplied bytes.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+- ASCII, non-Latin text, supplementary-plane characters, and combining sequences round-trip through `writeString`.
+- The committed blob bytes exactly equal `utf8.encode(input)`.
+- Raw byte writes preserve the caller-supplied bytes unchanged.
+
